@title Car Battler Joe (USA)
@file Car Battler Joe (U) [!].gba
@game ACBE
@chip EEPROM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@save skip: no save found up to Takah's figure-8 driving practice, which ends only when every item on the course has been picked up in real time (nba already loads it late, so its drive would differ); the first save lies somewhere beyond it. The field menu (Item, LRG cargo, Overdrive, Switch WPN, Status, Settings) has no Save and the title Settings write nothing; the only EEPROM write is the 58-byte header at first boot (identical in all three)
# Begin New Game, name "Joe", the intro by A every 30 frames, the practice
# battle lost by standing still, G-COM named "Pal", the next morning, then
# on foot past the water tower to the JOB office, Takah's briefing, and the
# first seconds of the figure-8 practice.
# Seen while recording: the shadows under sprites are drawn on alternate
# frames, and which frames differs between the three (a frame of game-loop
# phase); the name-entry backdrop is pink on dingbat-bios and mgba and green
# on nba (and the other way round on G-COM's naming screen); the town's
# wandering NPCs stand in different places on each emulator. nba runs the
# loading into the practice late: at practice_prompt (f24760) it is still
# typing Takah's "Are you ready" while the others show the Yes / Tell me
# once more choice, and it reached "OK, start!" 28 frames after them. At
# field_menu the two references agree and every dingbat configuration is
# the same picture 7 (mgba) / 5 (nba) frames off (shadow phase and Pal's
# step), within the hash window.

